03:51","previous":"10:03:05","deltaSeconds":46}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":28,"finishersRank":33,"finishRateRank":82,"winningTimeRank":4,"winningTimeRankDir":4,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2009 Comrades Marathon was the 84th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.170 km. The race was held on Sunday, 24 May. Conditions: Cool and cloudy early morning. Pleasantly warm with soft breeze mid afternoon. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nStephen MUZHINGI claimed the men's title in 05:23:27, ahead of Leonid SHVETSOV (05:33:10) and Charles Tjiane (05:34:21). Olesya NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:12:12, followed by Elena NURGALIEVA (06:13:14).\n\nOlesya NURGALIEVA's 06:12:12 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 12,945 entries, 10,008 runners crossed the finish line (77.3% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 8,264 men and 1,744 women (17.4% female). The average finish time was 10:03:51.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 11 Wally Hayward, 549 Silver, 1,936 Bill Rowan, 4,706 Bronze, 2,786 Vic Clapham. 1,986 runners (19.8%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Jerry MBOWENI in 11:59:59.\n\nThis edition featured the 4th fastest winning time on record. Compared to the previous down run in 2007, the field was 7.9% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 53% of the finishers, with 4,744 seniors (avg 09:45:11) and 5,264 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}